      "writtenOn": "2019-02-16T00:29:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is unnecessarily tricky, the globalScope.Set(k, v) is causing the evaluation of $(BUILD_SHARED_LIBRARY) to be cc_library_shared, and then it is treating include cc_library_shared as makeModule(\"cc_library_shared\").  Maybe instead this should be:\n\nvar soongModuleTypes \u003d map[string]string{\n\t\"BUILD_SHARED_LIBRARY\":        \"cc_library_shared\",\n\t...\n\t\"test/vts/tools/build/Android.host_config.mk\": \"vts_config\",\n}\nfor k, v :\u003d range moduleTypes {\n\tglobalScope.Set(k, k)\n}\n\nThen $(BUILD_SHARED_LIBRARY) will just resolve to BUILD_SHARED_LIBRARY, and you can look up BUILD_SHARED_LIBRARY or test/vts/tools/build/Android.host_config.mk in soongModuleTypes to get \"cc_library_shared\" or \"vts_config\".",
      "range": {
